# Table row actions

Do not put multiple action icon buttons in a trailing table column. Use a single **3-dot (⋮) context menu in the first (leftmost) column** of each row, matching GrovLink.

## Component

Use `app-row-actions-menu` from `admin/src/app/ui/row-actions-menu/row-actions-menu.component.ts`.

```typescript
import {
  RowActionsMenuComponent,
  RowActionItem,
} from '../../ui/row-actions-menu/row-actions-menu.component';

getRowActions(row: MyRow): RowActionItem[] {
  return [
    { id: 'edit', label: 'Edit', icon: 'pi pi-pencil', command: () => this.edit(row) },
    { id: 'delete', label: 'Delete', icon: 'pi pi-trash', severity: 'danger', command: () => this.confirmDelete(row) },
  ];
}
```

```html
<p-table [value]="rows()">
  <ng-template pTemplate="header">
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 3rem"></th>
      <th>Name</th>
      <!-- other columns — no trailing actions column -->
    </tr>
  </ng-template>
  <ng-template pTemplate="body" let-row>
    <tr>
      <td>
        <app-row-actions-menu [items]="getRowActions(row)" />
      </td>
      <td>{{ row.name }}</td>
    </tr>
  </ng-template>
</p-table>
```

## Rules

- First column: narrow (`width: 3rem`), holds only the menu trigger
- Menu trigger: vertical ellipsis (`pi-ellipsis-v`), not horizontal
- Destructive actions: `severity: 'danger'`; disable/enable toggles: `severity: 'warn'`
- Define actions in a `getRowActions(row)` method on the page component
- Do not add a right-side column of `p-button` icons for row actions
